-- title:
--   Additive bound for the cost of the Fermat-ring convolution program
-- statement:
--   For HvdH parameters $q$ with $P\ge 1$ and $K\ge 1$ and all $kb, Φ_m$, with $T = 2^{\mathrm{logOuter}}\cdot r$,
--   $$\mathrm{fwCost}(q,kb,Φ_m) \le 10^9 K\bigl(T(P+1)(e+kb+1) + 2^{\mathrm{logOuter}}(kb+1)^2\bigr) + 2^{\mathrm{logOuter}}Φ_m.$$
--   So the Fermat-ring convolution costs $O(K\,T\,P\,(e+kb))$ machine steps plus one recursive multiplication per Fermat-ring coefficient.
--
--   **Formalization Note.** `fwCost` is the explicit cost of `fwP` (sum of the encoding, transform-pass, pointwise-product, decoding and move costs `encCost`, `passCost`, `pmCost`, `dcCost`).
-- source:
--   D. Harvey, J. van der Hoeven, Integer multiplication in time O(n log n), Ann. of Math. 193 (2021), 563–617 (Theorem 1.1: multitape Turing machine multiplication in O(n log n)). Lemma `NLogN.FW.fwCost_le_add` of the Lean development NLogN/HFW11.lean (lines 32–42), written for the prove2.me integer-multiplication campaign.

-- Harvey–van der Hoeven multitape-TM development (NLogN), generated by skeleton subtraction.

import Definitions.Def_IntMul_HvdH_M_Defs4

set_option autoImplicit false
